@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_PORT_VERSION@-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Install > Package and Remove > Package show Ubuntu's logo (Nerd Font
    linux-ubuntu) instead of Arch's (md-arch): the entries install from
    Ubuntu's archive.
  * Install > Snap and Install > Flatpak pick apps from the Snap Store and
    Flathub in fzf, as Install > Package does from Ubuntu's archive; the
    Snap picker searches first and asks before installing a classic snap.
    Remove > Snap and Remove > Flatpak list the installed apps.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:00:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261014.23.d1c146fc-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * The menu answers its "is this package installed" tests from dpkg
    instead of pacman. With no pacman the menu took every package for
    absent: Install entries showed for installed programs (Chromium) and
    every Remove entry was hidden.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261014.22.8a7a6b3a-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * @DISTRO_ID@-desktop depends on localsend, as Omarchy preinstalls it:
    the Share menu and Files' "Send via LocalSend" have it to call. The
    package comes from this distro's repository (packages/localsend).
  * LocalSend's window rule and Files' "Send via LocalSend" extension are
    back; @DISTRO_ID@-config seeds the extension for new users and the
    port's first migration copies it for existing ones.
  * yt-dlp is back in the package list, with the native messaging host
    Chromium's Download Video extension calls; the migration registers
    the host for an existing user who has Chromium.
  * d/rules: copy migrations/ into the renamed tree, so the port's
    migrations reach the package (none was shipped before this one).

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261014.20.0559194c-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Upstream version +git<date>.<count>.<commit> instead of +git<date>:
    the fork's commit count since the Omarchy tag orders several fork
    changes in one day, and the hash names the commit. Same fork commit
    as 4.0.4+git20261014-0@DISTRO_ID@1.
  * @DISTRO_ID@-config installs /etc/chromium.d/zz-@DISTRO_ID@-user-flags,
    which makes the Debian Chromium launcher read the user's
    ~/.config/chromium-flags.conf, as Arch's wrapper does: Omarchy's flags
    and its three bundled extensions now apply to Chromium.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:45:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261014-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Install > Development installs build-essential (and unzip for OCaml)
    before building a toolchain: the image has no compiler.
  * Agents and mise tools from npm install Node.js first: the image has
    no Node.js.
  * Web apps use the first installed Chromium-based browser, and show a
    notification naming Install > Browser when there is none.
  * Steam and Lutris install the 32-bit Mesa and NVIDIA graphics drivers
    through the new hidden @DISTRO_ID@-install-32bit-graphics, since apt
    here installs no Recommends.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:30:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261013-0@DISTRO_ID@2) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * @DISTRO_ID@-desktop depends on ffmpegthumbnailer, so Files shows video
    thumbnails out of the box; it moved from the optional
    @DISTRO_ID@-desktop-apps, which keeps evince and gnome-disk-utility.
  * Drop the Suggests on intel-media-va-driver-non-free:
    @DISTRO_ID@-session depends on it since 0.1.4.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@+git20261013-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Version scheme: the upstream version is the Omarchy tag plus the date of
    the fork commit the packages are built from (+git<YYYYMMDD>), so every
    change to the fork has its own orig tarball; under the tag alone two
    revisions shared one orig tarball name with different contents.
  * New @DISTRO_ID@-launch-dgpu: runs a command on the discrete GPU of a
    hybrid-graphics machine, through @DISTRO_ID@-launch-nvidia on NVIDIA and
    with DRI_PRIME set to the AMD GPU's PCI address on AMD. The menu's
    launcher (@DISTRO_ID@-launch-desktop) uses it for entries that ask for the
    discrete GPU and for applications listed in ~/.config/@DISTRO_ID@/dgpu-apps
    (nvidia-apps, the list's first name, is still read), on NVIDIA and AMD
    machines alike. @DISTRO_ID@-debug-launch shows the offload variables
    (docs/7 choice 43).
  * The port changes made since the first build, from the fork's branch
    (2026-10-10 to 2026-10-13): the Plymouth theme and its passphrase hint,
    the migrations runner, packages added to the base list (plymouth-label,
    pulseaudio-utils, gawk, libgtk-3-bin, thermald, intel-lpmd,
    lsp-plugins-lv2), the login screen's user fallback, mise for the
    commands that need it, the balanced default power profile, the
    installer's window rule, @DISTRO_ID@-debug-launch, applications on the
    display GPU's Mesa driver on hybrid graphics with
    @DISTRO_ID@-launch-nvidia, and the menu's discrete-GPU choice.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0500

@DISTRO_ID@-desktop (@OMARCHY_VERSION@-0@DISTRO_ID@1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Omarchy @OMARCHY_TAG@ ported from Arch Linux to Ubuntu
    (roadmap step 6). One source, five binary packages: @DISTRO_ID@-desktop
    (metapackage, dependency list from the ported package list),
    @DISTRO_ID@-tools (the commands and install scripts), @DISTRO_ID@-shell
    (the Quickshell shell and icon font), @DISTRO_ID@-themes (theme bundles
    and templates) and @DISTRO_ID@-config (Hyprland defaults, /etc/skel seeds,
    session variables, units, drop-ins, SDDM theme, session file, Plymouth
    theme files, launchers and branding placeholders). Built from the port
    branch of the fork named in distro.conf, renamed at build time.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
